; FIBONACCI PAST THE PORTABLE WINDOW -- the program ADR 0019's refusal quotes.
;
; bounded.go's error message names this exact program:
;
;   fib(100)  Go   3736710778780434371     wrapped at int64
;             Java 3736710778780434371     wrapped at int64
;             JS   354224848179262000000   binary64, precision lost
;             true 354224848179261915075
;
; One source, three answers, none of them right. `examples/int/fib.oro` is the
; same program WITHOUT a declaration and is refused, which is the point of it.
; This one declares a result above the window, which is ADR 0019's third escape,
; and gets the true answer on every target that declares a bignum.
;
; THE DECLARATION IS ON THE RESULT AND NOTHING ELSE, which is what makes this the
; witness for a BIDIRECTIONAL solver. Every input is small -- `n` is at most 1000
; -- and nothing flowing forward makes `a` or `b` big. The pressure comes from
; the declared result, backwards through the loop's exit and then along the back
; edge: `a` is returned, so `a` is big; `(again b …)` assigns `b` to `a`, so `b`
; is big; and `i` is provably 0..1000, so `i` stays a machine word.
;
; fib(1000) has 209 digits and 2^1000 is a comfortable bound for it. The endpoint
; is an EXPRESSION rather than a literal, which is what the range language gained
; on 2026-08-31: it is evaluated and never emitted, so `KInt` stays an int64.
;
; THE BOUND IS FINITE ON PURPOSE. `(int 0 +inf)` would compile and give the same
; answer today, and it says something weaker: a finite range has a LIMB COUNT,
; which is a `build` of known length and zero allocations, where an unbounded one
; must fall back to whatever arbitrary precision the target ships. That rung is
; not built yet, so the two are indistinguishable in the emitted code -- but the
; declaration is the place the difference is said, and saying it now costs
; nothing.

; NO `(use …)` AT ALL, and that is the promotion of integer arithmetic to the
; language showing: `+` and `>=` are the language's names, found per target, so
; this file names no host. It generates on Go, JavaScript and the JVM unchanged.
(export fib)

(sig fib ((n (int 0 1000))) (int 0 (pow 2 1000)))

(def fib (fn (n)
  (loop ((a 0) (b 1) (i 0))
    (>= i n)  a
    else      (again b (+ a b) (+ i 1)))))
